      "ruins": 0.07,
      "hills": 0.04,
      "house": 0.05,
      "shop": 0.05,
      "field": 0.0,
      "road": -0.02
    },
    "slowEnemyBonus": 0.08,
    "nightBonus": 0.04,
    "//flee": "FLEE rolls this chance after every move away; BACK AWAY never rolls it and never ends the fight, it only holds the gap at distance.escapeSteps. Standing at that furthest distance adds maxDistanceBonus to a FLEE, and lifts the cap to maxChanceAtMaxDistance.",
    "maxDistanceBonus": 0.45,
    "maxChanceAtMaxDistance": 0.9,
    "//split": "What one FLEE is worth is split: escapeShare of it gets you away for good, and the rest of it wins you groundStep more steps instead, so an attempt that does not free you still leaves you better placed. A fight is therefore usually worth a blow or two before the ground is yours.",
    "escapeShare": 0.5,
    "groundStep": 1,
    "//wind": "Getting away is run, scramble and go to ground, and a body with no wind does all three badly: the chance is multiplied by staminaFloor at nothing left, rising to the whole of it at full stamina. A flee also costs fleeStaminaMultiplier times what the same move away costs when it is only BACK AWAY.",
    "staminaFloor": 0.6,
    "fleeStaminaMultiplier": 1.15,
    "//fleeStamina": "Prologue rule (27.09.2026): one FLEE attempt costs between min (fit, fed, rested, unhurt) and max stamina (at the worst of hunger, thirst, tiredness and wounds), so it stays about the same through a fight. Each level of the listed skills (dodge, athletics = swimming) takes perSkillLevel of it off, down to floorShare. Run or walk, whatever is held or carried: the weapon and the load change the steps an attempt covers, never its price. fleeStaminaMultiplier is no longer read.",
