    "//": "Loosing a shot or a throw while giving ground: the same action also walks a step back and then looses, so a survivor with a bow can hold the gap open instead of choosing between shooting and keeping away. It costs extra move points and some accuracy, and it is always a walk - nobody runs and looses at once. With no room left to give, the shot is taken standing and costs nothing extra.",
